<title>INDIA: India's BPL 1996/97 net rises.</title>
<headline>India's BPL 1996/97 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  484.70  vs     473.30</p>
<p>    Gross sales    12,906.00  vs  11,803.80</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)    18.02  vs	17.61</p>
<p>    Profit before     978.00  vs     870.70</p>
<p>interest, tax &amp;</p>
<p>depreciation</p>
<p>    Tax		   128.10  vs     135.00</p>
<p>Note: Television maker BPL Ltd said domestic sale of colour television sets rose to 523,572 units during the year (representing a market share of 29 percent) from 473,256 units (a market share of 26.3 percent) in the previous year.</p>
<p>BPL said it exported 38,856 units in 1996/97, making it India's largest colour television firm. The black and white television business grew by 35 percent. The total television sales of the firm crossed one million units at 10,18,710.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
